WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.109
Old Town Criterium follows a real place: the streets of Bruges.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.577
While the world draws, the race offers to stream the real Bruges, from Steenstraat

00:00:15.577 --> 00:00:19.080
to the Markt, as Google's photorealistic 3D Tiles.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:26.207
Paste your own Google Maps Platform key. It stays on this device, and goes only to

00:00:26.207 --> 00:00:30.101
Google's Map Tiles API, never to Telo Ride's backend.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.629
If Google refuses the key, the panel says so, and the built-in world stays.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:45.849
Accepted, the tiles stream beside the world, and the panel credits Google for what's

00:00:45.849 --> 00:00:46.583
in view.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.394
From a phone to a desktop, the offer sits above the race, clear of every panel.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.563
What the tests prove: the key reaches Google and nowhere else, a refusal keeps the

00:01:06.563 --> 00:01:10.075
world, and a stored key waits for you to press Stream it.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.869
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:17.214 --> 00:01:21.726
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.397
every hill and interval.

00:01:23.742 --> 00:01:28.920
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:34.368
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:37.358
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:40.196
A custom workout lives under Profile.
